      "data": {
        "text": "**Defining the Provider**\n\nI've decided to move forward with Google Cloud Vertex AI as the specific external provider. I need to make it clearly identifiable within the `select_platform_resource.py` file, which will resolve models, deployments, or inference resources.\n\n\n**Specifying the Resource**\n\nOkay, I've selected Vertex AI, and now I'm working to make it identifiable in the file, by using `google.cloud.aiplatform` within the code. I'm focusing on the `select_platform_resource.py` file, and I'm designing a function within it. That function, tentatively named `select_vertex_ai_model_resource`, will take the required Vertex AI parameters, such as project, location, and model/endpoint IDs. This function will then return either the resource path string or a client object. I think returning the path will be enough for now.\n\n\n**Drafting the Module**\n\nI'm now drafting the `select_platform_resource.py` file, incorporating the `select_vertex_ai_model_resource` function. This function will use `google.cloud.aiplatform` to resolve Vertex AI resources. I've decided to return a resource path string, which will simplify the initial implementation. I'm focusing on crafting the function signature, and also how to construct the Vertex AI resource name string. I'll include the import statement: `from google.cloud import aiplatform` and start there.\n\n\n",
        "time": {
          "end": 1789866988585,
          "start": 1789866985433
        },
        "type": "reasoning"
      },
